# Pull request review

There is **no** requirement to install or run the **CodeRabbit** or **Codex** command-line tools before **`git push`**. Use ordinary GitHub pull-request review and any optional checks configured on the repository.

If you change **versioning** wording in **`.coderabbit.yaml`**, keep **AGENTS.md**, **CLAUDE.md**, **`docs/versioning.md`**, and **`.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc`** aligned.

**CodeRabbit and `version_def.h`:** **`.coderabbit.yaml`** instructs reviewers to inspect **PR commit history** before flagging **`userland/shell/version_def.h`** — a header change in a commit by **`github-actions[bot]`** (author and committer) with the workflow’s own subject is not flagged, and the comment asks QA to confirm `./scripts/gen_version_def.sh --stdout | diff - userland/shell/version_def.h` with the generator and `scripts/lib` unchanged against the base (`.cursor/agents/devops-quality-engineer.md`, item 2); author and subject alone prove nothing, and a hand-edited header or non-automation commit is flagged. PRs opened by the **Version lock on merge** action (subject **`chore(version): sync version/locked from entries after merge`**, branch `cursor/version-lock-from-entries-*`; its author and committer are not necessarily the bot) follow the **Automation version PRs** policy (no proactive review), not this rule.
